  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Rotary Parallel now reads the setup stock.\n- An end of the model is a held end when the stock goes on past it by more than one tool diameter (plus the tolerance). This is a bar that goes on into a chuck or onto a centre.\n- At a held end the centre of the ball does not go past the end plane of the model. The end face is not cut. The turned surface is finished to its end.\n- The operation adds a note that names the end: `Rotary Parallel: the stock goes on 19.050 mm past the end of the model at (-31.750, 0.000, 0.000) - that end face is left, and the tool stops at its plane`.\n- Under the sloped-entry law, a ramp does not start past a held end. That infeed stays a radial plunge.\n- A model with no length between two held ends is refused by name.\n- A free end is cut as before. Stock that goes on by one tool diameter or less is a facing allowance and is cut as before.\n- The #1904 example project and program are generated again. The two guide pages and the two pictures follow the new program. The guide page drops its \"air cut only\" limit and keeps the air cut as the first run.\n\nNew code:\n\n- `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary_ends.rs` (new): `held` reads the two ends, `clip` keeps the cutting moves in the window.\n- `rotary_parallel_in(facets, stock, params, axis)` in `rotary.rs`. `rotary_parallel` calls it with no stock.\n- `rotary_links::Ramp` has the field `span`.\n- `generate.rs` passes the stock facets (one line).\n\n## Cause\n\n`rotary_parallel` ran the finishing raster over the whole model and did not know the stock. The pass down the chuck-side end face was a slot one tool diameter wide from the skin of the bar to its axis.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `camcraft-app` `continuous_4axis_part::the_pass_leaves_the_chuck_side_end_face` (replaces `the_pass_cuts_the_chuck_side_end_face_to_the_centreline`). Red on unchanged code: `the tool passes the chuck-side end plane: X-1.3171`.\n- `camcraft-app` `continuous_4axis_part::a_short_flute_posts_now_that_the_chuck_side_end_face_is_left` (replaces `a_short_flute_is_blocked_at_the_chuck_side_end_face`). The shank refusal came from the cut that is gone.\n- `camcraft-motion` `rotary::the_parallel_leaves_the_end_face_where_the_stock_goes_on`: held end, free end, sloped entries, facing allowance, flush stock.\n- `camcraft-motion` lib `multiaxis::rotary_ends::tests` (3 tests): the window, the refusal, the clip.\n- `site/tests/test_first_continuous_4axis_part.py`: 14 tests pass.\n\nThe `#[test]` count of `continuous_4axis_part` is the same (9).\n\nMutation results:\n\n| Mutation | Pin | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| The clip is off (`rotary.rs`) | `the_parallel_leaves_the_end_face_where_the_stock_goes_on` | red: `the ball center passed the held end's plane: station -1.014` |\n| The clip is off | `the_pass_leaves_the_chuck_side_end_face` | red: `X-1.3171` |\n| The clip is off | `a_short_flute_posts_now_that_the_chuck_side_end_face_is_left` | red: `post blocked - 23 warning(s): Journal: shank/holder at move 1380 collides with the uncut stock` |\n| The ramp guard is off (`rotary_links.rs`) | `the_parallel_leaves_the_end_face_where_the_stock_goes_on` | red: `a ramp runs in from past the plane` (from station -8.03) |\n| `generate.rs` as on main (no stock passed) | `the_pass_leaves_the_chuck_side_end_face` | red: `X-1.3171` |\n\nEach pin is green with the fix restored.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 129 steps, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean on the final head.\n\nThe gate ran before two clippy fixes in `rotary_ends.rs` (a `partial_cmp` in place of a negated comparison, and one doc comment line). After them, these ran green on the final head: the `rotary_ends` lib tests, the `rotary` and `rotary_links` suites, the `continuous_4axis_part` suite and the site page test.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nOne: `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.nc` (3213 lines to 3125 lines). `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` holds the same toolpath as its cache.\n\n- 1306 `G1` lines past the chuck-side plane (X below -1.25) are gone. These are the end-face cut.\n- 1210 `G0` lines and 42 `G1` lines are new at the chuck-side end (X-1.25 to X-1.15). These are the retract, the A index on the clearance radius and the plunge of each pass.\n- 21 `G1` lines at the chuck-side end are gone: the passes now stop at X-1.25.\n- About 12 lines in other places differ. The `G93` or `G94` word is on a different line of the same moves, or an A or F word differs in the last digit.\n- The free end is the same: the lowest Z at X above 0 is -0.0322 before and after.\n- The project file version goes from 70 to 71. Main moved the format after the example was written.\n- No snapshot PNG changed. No other `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No machine run and no PathPilot simulator run of the new program.\n- A model with a domed or coned held end. The rule keeps the centre of the ball inside the end plane, but the pass still cuts that dome or cone up to the plane.\n- A bar with two held ends in the app (the kernel unit test has it).\n- A tilted fitted axis with a stock: the test bars lie along X.\n- The kit golden `wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc` does not change. Its stock ends where its model ends, so CamCraft reads air there. The guide pages now say that the stock must be as long as the bar.\n- No new setting (an axial window). That is a `feat` and needs a parameter, a project-file version, a UI field and an MCP field. `docs/decisions/2343-rotary-parallel-held-end.md` has the reasons. No follow-up issue is filed for it.\n- No new command, so no MCP tool.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2563 touches `crates/app/tests/continuous_4axis_part.rs` (the import line and `build_with`) and `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj`. It touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. The second one must generate the example project again (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`).\n- #2149 and #1713 touch `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` in other arms. This PR changes one line in the rotary arm.\n\nChangelog: Rotary Parallel leaves the end face of the model where the stock goes on past it (a bar held in a chuck), and a note names that end; before, it cut that end face to the axis and parted the bar (#2343).\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #2343\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
